Do not reinit the drivers on SET_SYSTEM_AV_INFO before main init has run.

mgba (mgba-emu tree) reports its audio rate from retro_load_game(), so
RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_SET_SYSTEM_AV_INFO arrives before retroarch_main_init()
has started any driver.  The handler's CMD_EVENT_REINIT brings every driver
up there and then, and main init's own drivers_init() opens the video driver
a second time without closing the first.  Elsewhere that leaks a window;
SDL's mali-fbdev backend allows one EGL window surface, so the second open
fails ("Can't create EGL window surface") and RetroArch exits.

main init reads av_info from the core again and initializes every driver
right after content loads, so before then storing av_info is enough.

--- a/runloop.c
+++ b/runloop.c
@@ -2702,6 +2702,12 @@
 
             memcpy(av_info, *info, sizeof(*av_info));
 
+            /* Called from retro_load_game(): retroarch_main_init() reads
+             * av_info again and starts every driver right after, so a reinit
+             * here only creates a second window over the first one. */
+            if (!(runloop_st->flags & RUNLOOP_FLAG_IS_INITED))
+               return true;
+
             command_event(CMD_EVENT_REINIT, &reinit_flags);
 
             if (no_video_reinit)
